  "notes": "The shuffle is a swing number, not a meter. Eighths swung at 64% put the in-between notes a little ahead of the 12/8 triplet — 614 ticks of a 960-tick beat against the triplet's 640 — which is the shuffle a drummer plays rather than the arithmetic one, and the whole kit is heard through it: kick on 1 and 3 in a two-beat, snare hard on 2 and 4, and a ride carrying the shuffled eighths above a thinned-out hat. The verse plays the backbeat as cross-stick and the chorus opens up to the full snare, which is the arrangement device the style is known for. Bass is boom-chick, root on the beat and fifth on the off; harmony is I–IV–V with a flat-seven and blues passing tones for colour. No 808 — this is a played kit.",
